SHELL
=====

Your command-line interface.


WHAT IT IS
----------
The shell is where you type commands.
It talks to your computer's operating system.


COMMON SHELLS
-------------
bash    Most common
zsh     Mac default, powerful
sh      Simple, everywhere


BASICS
------
pwd             Where am I?
ls              List files
cd folder       Enter folder
cd ..           Go up one level
mkdir name      Create folder
rm file         Delete file


NAVIGATION
----------
~               Home directory
.               Current directory
..              Parent directory
/               Root directory


SPECIAL KEYS
------------
Tab             Auto-complete
Ctrl+C          Stop command
Ctrl+D          Exit shell
Up/Down arrows  Command history


PIPES & REDIRECTION
-------------------
command > file      Save output to file
command >> file     Append to file
command1 | command2 Pipe output


